    "user_request_original": "Design a 21-layer defect-cavity dielectric stack on fused silica substrate using HfO2 and SiO2. Stack topology: Air | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2_cavity | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | Fused Silica. Layer 11 (index 10, HfO2 cavity) thickness initialization: center at 295 nm with variance ±25 nm. Apply neighboring-layer coupling penalty with weight 0.05 between layers 9-10-11 to discourage discontinuous thickness jumps. Optimize all 21 layer thicknesses for maximum transmission in 1000-1700 nm and maximum reflection in 300-450 nm at normal incidence. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with convergence tolerance tightened to address numerical convergence issues. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1000-1700 nm; transmission in 300-450 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum total layer count of 30.",
